message:
I see - line 369's `grid_points[1]` is in the `mft_CommonLayout` struct, which is the layout of the ICC tag data itself (the input file format). The `skcms_A2B` struct in the header has `grid_points[4]`. So the vulnerability is different.

Let me re-read the code. In `read_mft_common`:
```c
a2b->input_channels  = mftTag->input_channels[0];
for (uint32_t i = 0; i < a2b->input_channels; ++i) {
    a2b->grid_points[i] = mftTag->grid_points[0];
}
```

The `a2b->grid_points` is `uint8_t grid_points[4]` in the header, so writing up to 4 elements is fine. But wait - the check `if (a2b->input_channels > ARRAY_COUNT(a2b->input_curves))` happens AFTER the loop. So if `input_channels` is > 4, the loop writes out of bounds to `a2b->grid_points[i]` for `i >= 4`.

Let me check `ARRAY_COUNT` and `input_curves`:

<｜｜DSML｜｜=execute_bash>
<parameter=command>grep -n "ARRAY_COUNT" /workspace/repo-vul/src-vul/skcms/src/ICCProfile.c | head -5 && echo "---" && grep -n "define ARRAY_COUNT" /workspace/repo-vul/src-vul/skcms/src/*.h /workspace/repo-vul/src-vul/skcms/src/*.c</｜｜DSML｜｜>
</｜｜DSML｜｜>

